Z||000000||FieroGT 914||05-25-2001||09:44 AM||||Hey, I'm new to the forum and I've got a headlight question concerning my 86GT.  the driver side headlight doesn't work properly... I have to turn the knob on the top of the motor, go back in the car, and then headlights work fine. They also go down fine but then the driver side headlight needs to have the knob rotated a little bit to have them work again. It's as though it over rotates on the way down and locks itself until it's manually turned a little.  Any ideas on what the problem is or how to fix it??? I tried some WD-40 underneath thinking it was just getting hung up but that didn't seem to work.  any help would be greatly apprectiated. thanks! <BR>-Joe<BR>White86GT<BR>'FieroGT 914'-aol||||reg||5
Z||000001||ROB MAC||05-25-2001||10:01 AM||||Could be the motor brushes are almost worn out, or the grease inside is getting gummy and binding, or the gear is worn, or the relay is bad. My guess is the brushes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||05-25-2001||11:21 AM||||Rodney Dickman (http://www.rodneydickman.com/index.html) has a rebuild kit for the headlights, not too expencive, and they come with very good instructions.||||reg||1
